# Revisions whose lines `git blame` should skip.
#
# 7ce3cf7 is the one-off `style: cargo fmt --all` commit: it reformatted the
# whole workspace for the first time, so it touches nearly every line of every
# file without changing behaviour. Without this file, every line it re-wrapped
# would be blamed on that commit instead of on the person who wrote the code,
# and line numbers would no longer match older history.
#
# Enable it once per clone (local config, not committed):
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Or per invocation: git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <file>
#
# Rules for this file: append-only, one full 40-character SHA per line, and
# only formatting/reordering commits — never anything that changed behaviour.
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored by git.

